    "fileId": 45015,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Oesophageal squamous dysplasia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A </strong>On low-magnification endoscopy with narrow-band imaging, the lesion appears as a brownish area about 10 mm in size on the front left wall and 300 mm from the incisors. <strong>B</strong> On high-magnification endoscopy with narrow-band imaging, the intrapapillary capillary loops are mildly irregular and the mucosa between them is brightly coloured. <strong>C</strong> On white-light endoscopy, the lesion appears flat and slightly depressed, with mild redness. <strong>D</strong> On Lugol&rsquo;s chromoendoscopy, the lesion is positive for the pink sign &ndash; it is well demarcated and unstained.",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Fujii S",
    "tablehtml": "",
